--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Saturday, the 3rd of January, 1931 (1/1 key facts kept) ---
I pawned the silver pencil for 9d., and stole a loaf of bread, nobody seeing.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Saturday, the 3rd of January, 1931 (1/1 key facts kept) ---
I resolved in future to finish all my ledgers completely before handing them in, never to let myself get into arrears with my work, spoke with Mr. Barker about what the paper says: There was little activity today in the great collieries of South Wales, where last night negotiations between the owners and the men were broken off, spoke with Police-Constable Dawe about what the paper says, and with Mrs. Nolan.

